[quote]"Look for flowers in a meadow? Do I look like a bee to you?"

Henry of Skalitz[/quote]

Alright, look. I'm a blacksmith's son. I can forge a sword, lose at dice, and get knocked flat by a man half my size. What I can't do, it turns out, is tell Sage from the forty other green things growing next to it.

And everyone wants herbs. Every herb woman, every alchemist, every lad with a cough. It's always nine of something, and it's always the something that looks exactly like grass. So I've spent a fair bit of this war bent over in a meadow, squinting. Very heroic, I know.

This mod sorts that out. The things worth picking are brighter, so they stand out from the things that aren't. And for when that isn't enough, there's a key that lights up the lot.

[center][img]IMAGE_URL_PULSE_OFF_ON[/img][/center]

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Herbs are brighter.[/b] All sixteen kinds you can pick: Belladonna, Chamomile, Comfrey, Dandelion, Eyebright, Feverfew, Herb Paris, Marigold, Mint, Nettle, Poppy, Sage, St. John's wort, Thistle, Valerian and Wormwood.[/*]
[*][b]Mushrooms too.[/b] Amanita muscaria (fly agaric), Boletus edulis (penny bun) and Lepiota (parasol).[/*]
[*][b]So are the other things people keep sending me after.[/b] Bird's nests, beehives, fish traps, buried treasure and graves. Aye, graves. Don't look at me like that.[/*]
[*][b]Everything else is left alone.[/b] Grass is still grass. The fungi on trees and the stork nests keep their usual look, since there's nothing in them for me anyway.[/*]
[/list]

It's the same plants in the same places, and nothing is added to the world. They're just easier to spot, for those of us who weren't raised by an apothecary.

[size=5][b]The pulse[/b][/size]

Still can't see them? Fine. Neither can I, half the time.

[list]
[*][b]Press F5.[/b] Everything the mod covers glows bright magenta for 30 seconds, then goes back to normal.[/*]
[*][b]Four of them glow gold instead:[/b] Herb Paris, St. John's wort, Wormwood and Amanita muscaria.[/*]
[*][b]Press it again[/b] while they're lit and the count starts over.[/*]
[/list]

Subtle it isn't. A proper herb woman would box my ears for it. But I've yet to see one find Wormwood any quicker.

[center][img]IMAGE_URL_PULSE_CLOSEUP[/img][/center]

