[size=5][b]Changing the key, the time and the colours[/b][/size]

There's a file called [font=Courier New]settings.cfg[/font] in the mod's folder. Open it in Notepad. I know, I know, reading. I only learned this year myself. But every line has a note above it, so you'll manage.

[list]
[*][b]The key:[/b] [font=Courier New]bind f5 brighter_forage_pulse[/font]
Change [font=Courier New]f5[/font] to another key, such as [font=Courier New]f6[/font], [font=Courier New]g[/font], [font=Courier New]np_1[/font] (number pad) or [font=Courier New]mouse4[/font]. Pick one the game doesn't already use, or pressing it does both things.[/*]
[*][b]How long it lasts:[/b] [font=Courier New]brighter_forage_seconds 30[/font]
Any number of seconds above 0. Much longer than 30 hasn't been tried, so you're on your own there.[/*]
[*][b]Each colour:[/b] [font=Courier New]brighter_forage_color sage magenta[/font]
One line per thing. Change the last word to [font=Courier New]magenta[/font], [font=Courier New]gold[/font], [font=Courier New]off[/font], or your own colour as three numbers with commas and no spaces, such as [font=Courier New]20,14,0[/font] (that one's gold).[/*]
[/list]

[list]
[*][b][font=Courier New]off[/font][/b] leaves that one out of the pulse. Handy if you're sick of the sight of Nettles. I am. They sting like the devil.[/*]
[*][b]Changes apply[/b] the next time you start the game.[/*]
[*][b]To apply them now,[/b] open the console with [font=Courier New]~[/font], type [font=Courier New]exec mods/brighter_forage/settings.cfg[/font] and press Enter. If you changed the key, the old one keeps working too until you restart. Two keys. Wonderful.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download the zip from the Files tab.[/*]
[*]Extract it into [font=Courier New]<game>\Mods\[/font], so you end up with [font=Courier New]<game>\Mods\brighter_forage\[/font]. Make the [font=Courier New]Mods[/font] folder if you don't have one.[/*]
[*]Start the game and go and find a meadow.[/*]
[/list]

[font=Courier New]<game>[/font] is where the game is installed. On Steam that's usually [font=Courier New]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\KingdomComeDeliverance2[/font].

To update, delete the old [font=Courier New]brighter_forage[/font] folder first, then put the new one in. If you changed [font=Courier New]settings.cfg[/font], keep a copy, or you'll be setting your colours again.

[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]

Delete [font=Courier New]<game>\Mods\brighter_forage[/font]. That's it. The mod keeps nothing in your saves, so the game goes back to how it was, and so do I. Squinting.

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Tested on game version 1.5.6 (Steam).[/b][/*]
[*][b]It won't get along with[/b] any other mod that changes the same plants, nests, hives, traps, sacks or graves, or one that uses the same key. That means other mods that make herbs or nests easier to see. Pick one or the other.[/*]
[*][b]Some things glow that you can't loot.[/b] A few nests and hives are only there for decoration, like the ones at a fisherman's stall, and they get brighter and pulse all the same. I've been fooled. More than once.[/*]
[*][b]The ground around buried treasure and graves[/b] gets brighter along with them. I'd call that a favour.[/*]
[*][b]Not everything's been looked at up close yet.[/b] I've seen the herbs with my own eyes, and they look right. The mushrooms and the rest pulse as they should, but I haven't gone round and looked at every one of them out in the world yet.[/*]
[*][b]After a game update,[/b] the mod may need a new version. If the herbs look wrong after a patch, take it out until there is one.[/*]
[*][b]It doesn't pick anything for you,[/b] carry it, or brew it. And it won't feed me either. I still feel quite hungry.[/*]
[*][b]It pairs well with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/kingdomcomedeliverance2/mods/4022]Instant Gather[/url].[/b] This one finds the herbs, that one picks them without all the kneeling. My back sends its thanks.[/*]
[/list]

God be with you. And if you do find the Belladonna, don't eat it.
